   "design": "Citations are written on a handheld that sends them to the case system, and photos taken on it attach to the case with time and place, so paper citations are not copied at the office and photos are not renamed and attached by hand. Questioning, checks, the decision, explaining, the report, signing, filing and the supervisor talk stay with the warden; no system decides on a warning or citation. The handheld records cases, not warden performance, and that use is agreed with the works council.",
   "previous_blocker": "Paper citations were retyped and photos attached by hand.",
   "enabler_now": "Handheld citation apps linked to the case system.",
   "still_hard": "Areas without signal.",
   "human_edge": "Deciding when a warning teaches more than a fine.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Less retyping; enforcement judgement stays.",
