   "approvals": [],
   "design": "One page lists the reserve rules by area and the current closures from the closure register, so the warden finds an answer in one place. An online answer desk on that page answers visitors' questions with a quote from the published rules, marked as AI, so fewer simple questions reach the warden by phone and mail; permits, fines and personal questions still go to the warden. Patrol conversations, notice boards, group talks and incident notes stay with the warden.",
   "previous_blocker": "Rules and closures were scattered, and every question came to the warden.",
   "enabler_now": "A single rules page fed by the closure register, with an answer desk.",
   "still_hard": "Visitors without phones in the reserve.",
   "human_edge": "Explaining why a rule protects a breeding bird.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Fewer repeat questions; patrol talks stay.",
   "reach": [
